ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.1257922079156626,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":94.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.057282429127598594,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":97.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.021711222174371297,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.010954566872818372,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":44.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11503640216184685,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":82.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10879025296931964,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.012593569734876131,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":65.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018381407625178516,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":69.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.1037,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":69.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.15,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":15.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Regional Management Corp., a diversified consumer finance company, provides various installment loan products primarily to customers with limited access to consumer credit from banks, thrifts, credit card companies, and other lenders in the United States. It offers small and large loans, and related payment and collateral protection insurance products. The company also provides optional payment and collateral protection insurance relating to its loan products, including credit life insurance, accidental and health insurance, involuntary unemployment insurance, and personal property insurance; and reinsurance services. In addition, its loans are sourced through branches, direct mail campaigns, digital partners, and consumer website. Regional Management Corp. was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Greer, South Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lakhbir S. Lamba | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $237,279 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $306K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $144K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Regional Management Corp. is a small-cap financial services business with a $319M market cap on $646M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $304M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 47 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.96\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.3pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (85% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 93% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"